  "body": "I'm a maintainer of the wasm-bindgen project, and discovered this one investigating buffer usage across web APIs.\n\nThe [`sendReport()`](https://wicg.github.io/webhid/#dom-hiddevice-sendreport) and [`sendFeatureReport()`](https://wicg.github.io/webhid/#dom-hiddevice-sendfeaturereport) method steps reference the `data` BufferSource argument inside \"Perform the following steps in parallel\" (\"Invoke the operating system to send an output report with the specified reportId and data\").\n\nThe result of this is that the spec as written does not guarantee exactly when the bytes are taken. HTML's event loop guidance advises against reading realm-associated objects in this way (https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-loop-for-spec-authors).\n\nWhile this could remain as-is, updating the the method steps gain an explicit \"[get a copy of the bytes held by the buffer source](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-get-buffer-source-copy) data\" step before the in-parallel steps, as [WebUSB does for `transferOut()`](https://wicg.github.io/webusb/#dom-usbdevice-transferout) for Web Bluetooth's `writeValue()` variants could be an option here.",
  "closed_by": null,
